<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main id="main">

  <%- include('partials/page-hero', {
    eyebrow: 'Legal',
    eyebrowIcon: 'clipboard',
    heroTitle: 'Terms of Service',
    heroIntro: 'The terms that govern cleaning services provided by Zenvorali Cleaning across the Kansas City metropolitan area — covering booking, access, cancellation, pricing, liability, our re-clean guarantee and payment conditions.',
    heroPoints: null,
    breadcrumbs: [{ name: 'Terms of Service', href: '/terms-of-service' }]
  }) %>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose prose--legal reveal">
        <p class="legal-meta"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 4 October 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Effective:</strong> 4 October 2026</p>

        <p>
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") form a binding agreement between you ("client", "you") and
          <strong><%= site.legalName %></strong> ("Zenvorali Cleaning", "we", "us"), located at
          <%= site.address.full %>. By booking a service, requesting a quote that you accept, or
          permitting our crew to begin work, you agree to these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          We have kept these terms as readable as we can. Where a clause limits liability or imposes an
          obligation on you, we have said so plainly rather than burying it.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Services Provided</h2>
        <p>
          We provide residential and commercial cleaning services in the Kansas City metropolitan area
          within approximately <%= site.serviceArea.radiusMiles %> miles of downtown Kansas City. Our
          current service lines are house cleaning, deep cleaning, move-in and move-out cleaning, apartment
          and condo cleaning, office and commercial cleaning, and post-construction cleaning.
        </p>
        <p>
          The specific scope of work for any booking is set out in the written quote we provide before
          work begins. <strong>The written quote forms part of these Terms.</strong> Where the quote and
          these Terms conflict regarding the scope of work, the quote prevails. Where they conflict on any
          other matter, these Terms prevail.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Quotations and Pricing</h2>
        <h3>2.1 Flat-rate quotes</h3>
        <p>
          All residential services are quoted at a flat rate, not an hourly rate. The quoted price is based
          on the property size, the number of bedrooms and bathrooms, the condition of the property, the
          frequency of service and any add-ons you select. Once you accept a quote, that price will not
          change unless you request additional work or the actual condition of the property differs
          materially from what we were shown or told.
        </p>
        <h3>2.2 Condition discrepancies</h3>
        <p>
          If we arrive and find the property in substantially worse condition than represented — for
          example, heavy build-up described as standard, undisclosed pet damage, or a hoarding situation —
          we will stop before starting and contact you. We will then either re-quote for the additional
          work or cancel the visit at no charge. We will never silently add charges to your invoice.
        </p>
        <h3>2.3 Add-ons</h3>
        <p>
          Add-on services such as inside-oven cleaning, inside-refrigerator cleaning, interior windows,
          carpet extraction, laundry and garage sweeping are priced separately. Nothing is added to your
          invoice without your prior approval.
        </p>
        <h3>2.4 No hidden fees</h3>
        <p>
          We do not charge fuel surcharges, travel fees or supplies charges anywhere within our service
          radius. The quoted figure is the invoiced figure.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Booking, Access and Scheduling</h2>
        <h3>3.1 Access</h3>
        <p>
          You agree to provide access to the property at the agreed time, whether by being present,
          providing a key, arranging a lockbox, providing a door code or notifying a concierge. If our crew
          cannot gain access within 30 minutes of the scheduled arrival time, the visit will be treated as
          a late cancellation under section 4.
        </p>
        <h3>3.2 Utilities</h3>
        <p>
          Running water and electricity must be available at the property. We cannot clean without them, and
          a visit where utilities are disconnected will be treated as a late cancellation.
        </p>
        <h3>3.3 Arrival windows</h3>
        <p>
          We schedule a two-hour arrival window and send a text notification when the crew is approximately
          20 minutes away. Traffic and weather in the Kansas City metro occasionally cause delay. We do not
          offer compensation for late arrival, but we will always contact you if a delay is expected.
        </p>
        <h3>3.4 Safety and conditions on site</h3>
        <p>
          You agree to inform us in advance of any hazards: aggressive pets, pest infestation, mould, bodily
          fluids, sharps, exposed wiring, unsafe flooring or any other condition that may endanger our crew.
          We reserve the right to decline or stop work where a genuine safety risk exists. Biohazard,
          hoarding, mould remediation and pest-infested properties are outside our scope and we will refer
          you to a specialist.
        </p>
        <h3>3.5 Pets</h3>
        <p>
          Please secure or inform us about pets. We are comfortable working around friendly animals, but we
          cannot clean safely around an anxious or aggressive pet. If a pet is not secured and our crew
          cannot work safely, the visit will be treated as a late cancellation.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cancellations and Rescheduling</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>More than 48 hours' notice:</strong> no charge. Reschedule freely.</li>
          <li><strong>24 to 48 hours' notice:</strong> no charge, though repeated rescheduling may affect your standing slot.</li>
          <li><strong>Less than 24 hours' notice, or no access:</strong> a fee of 50% of the quoted price applies, because the slot cannot be refilled at that notice.</li>
          <li><strong>Recurring plans:</strong> you may pause or cancel a recurring plan at any time with 48 hours' notice. There is no cancellation fee and no minimum term.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If we cancel or fail to attend a scheduled visit for any reason within our control, no charge
          applies and we will offer the earliest available replacement slot.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Payment Terms</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Residential clients are charged on the day of service, unless otherwise agreed in writing.</li>
          <li>We accept major credit and debit cards, ACH bank transfer and Apple Pay.</li>
          <li>Commercial clients receive consolidated monthly invoicing with payment due within 30 days of invoice date.</li>
          <li>Post-construction contracts over $2,000 carry a 25% mobilisation deposit, credited against the first invoice.</li>
          <li>Invoices unpaid after 30 days may incur interest at 1.5% per month or the maximum permitted by law, whichever is lower.</li>
          <li>Bank charges incurred through failed or reversed payments may be passed on to you.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. The Zenvorali Re-Clean Guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          If any item on the agreed written scope has not been completed to a reasonable professional
          standard, notify us <strong>within 24 hours of the visit</strong> and we will return and correct
          that item at no additional charge, including travel. This is your primary remedy for
          unsatisfactory work.
        </p>
        <p>The guarantee does not apply where:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Notification is received more than 24 hours after the visit.</li>
          <li>The property has been used or altered since our visit, or other trades have worked in the area.</li>
          <li>The item was outside the agreed scope of work.</li>
          <li>The condition results from pre-existing damage, wear, staining or a defect in materials — for example permanent grout discolouration or etched stone from an earlier cleaning product.</li>
          <li>The request concerns an outcome that professional cleaning cannot reasonably achieve, such as removing paint from a porous surface applied years ago.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Damage, Liability and Insurance</h2>
        <h3>7.1 Our insurance</h3>
        <p>
          We carry $2,000,000 in general liability insurance, workers' compensation for all employees, and
          bonding cover. Certificates of insurance are available on request.
        </p>
        <h3>7.2 Reporting damage</h3>
        <p>
          Any damage must be reported to us <strong>within 24 hours of the visit</strong>. We photograph
          the condition of unusual items on arrival where practical, which helps resolve claims quickly and
          fairly. Claims reported later are difficult to attribute and may be declined.
        </p>
        <h3>7.3 Limitation of liability</h3>
        <p>
          Our total liability arising out of any single visit is limited to the amount charged for that
          visit, except in cases of our negligence causing personal injury or property damage, where our
          liability is limited to the extent of our insurance cover, or where limitation is prohibited by
          law. We are not liable for:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pre-existing damage, wear or deterioration.</li>
          <li>Damage to items that were already broken, loose, unstable or improperly installed — including unsecured shelving, loose taps, damaged grout and failing seals.</li>
          <li>Damage caused by a defect in the surface or material itself, such as a finish that lifts when cleaned by normal methods.</li>
          <li>Indirect or consequential losses, including loss of profit, loss of use or loss of opportunity.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>7.4 Items of special value</h3>
        <p>
          Please inform us in advance about fragile items, antiques, artwork, irreplaceable objects or
          items of significant value so we can handle them appropriately or exclude them from the scope. We
          do not accept liability for items which were not disclosed and which could not reasonably have
          been identified as fragile.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate information about the property's size, condition and layout when requesting a quote.</li>
          <li>Disclose hazards, fragile items and items of special value before the visit.</li>
          <li>Secure pets and provide safe access.</li>
          <li>Ensure utilities are connected.</li>
          <li>Secure cash, jewellery, firearms and confidential documents. We ask our crew not to handle these; please place them out of scope.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Keys, Alarm Codes and Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>
          Where you provide a key or alarm code, it is stored in a locked cabinet with logged sign-out
          procedures and is deleted within 30 days of your final service or on request. Our employees sign
          confidentiality agreements and receive training on client privacy. We do not disclose your
          address, identity or personal details to third parties except as described in our
          <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Photographs</h2>
        <p>
          Our crew may photograph completed work for quality assurance and, in the case of move-out and
          commercial work, to provide documentation to you or your property manager. We will not publish
          identifiable photographs of your property, address or belongings for marketing purposes without
          your prior written consent.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Non-Solicitation of Staff</h2>
        <p>
          You agree not to directly employ or engage any Zenvorali Cleaning employee to perform cleaning
          services for you privately, during their employment with us or for 12 months afterwards. Our
          staff are employed, trained and insured at significant cost, and direct engagement circumvents
          the insurance and vetting protections that exist for your benefit as much as ours.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Force Majeure</h2>
        <p>
          We are not liable for failure to perform where the failure results from events outside our
          reasonable control, including severe weather, flooding, ice storms, utility failure, road
          closures, illness affecting a crew, or governmental restrictions. In such circumstances we will
          contact you promptly and reschedule at no charge.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Complaints and Dispute Resolution</h2>
        <p>
          If you are unhappy with any aspect of our service, please contact us first at
          <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a> or
          <a href="<%= site.phoneHref %>"><%= site.phone %></a>. We will acknowledge your complaint within
          two business days and aim to resolve it within ten. Most issues are resolved through the re-clean
          guarantee. If we cannot resolve a dispute directly, both parties agree to attempt mediation in
          Jackson County, Missouri before commencing legal proceedings.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Missouri. Any legal proceedings must be
          brought in the state or federal courts located in Jackson County, Missouri, and both parties
          consent to the jurisdiction of those courts.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Severability and Entire Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue
          in full force. These Terms, together with your written quote and our
          <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, constitute the entire agreement between us and
          supersede any prior discussions.
        </p>

        <h2>16. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. The version in force at the time of your booking
          governs that booking. Material changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above and,
          where significant, notified to active clients by email.
        </p>

        <h2>17. Contact</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a></li>
          <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="<%= site.phoneHref %>"><%= site.phone %></a></li>
          <li><strong>Post:</strong> <%= site.legalName %>, <%= site.address.line1 %>, <%= site.address.city %>, <%= site.address.state %> <%= site.address.zip %></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/cta', {
    ctaEyebrow: 'Plain-English answers',
    ctaTitle: 'Prefer to Talk Through the Details?',
    ctaText: 'If any clause here affects your booking and you would like it explained, call us. A real person will go through it with you.'
  }) %>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<button class="to-top" id="toTop" type="button" aria-label="Back to top"><%- icon('chevronDown', 22) %></button>
